A replace directive naming a version of a module the target imports, replaced by
another version of the same module, so that the build list is read for a
replacement that is a module rather than a directory. The replacement is the
version this repository's own go.mod requires, so the module cache holds it
when the test loads with GOPROXY=off.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27.1

require golang.org/x/mod v0.40.0

replace golang.org/x/mod v0.40.0 => golang.org/x/mod v0.43.0
-- go.sum --
golang.org/x/mod v0.43.0 h1:MFuq5J6s35W9D3IjkwyWc9vHh0nENOrt5K8Iof4ofmg=
golang.org/x/mod v0.43.0/go.mod h1:4ec1JnuyBz5+FIVhg86UsA39YG8BpnrZdJYSNHmGzHY=
-- app.go --
package app

import "golang.org/x/mod/semver"

// Newer reports whether version a sorts after version b.
func Newer(a, b string) bool { return semver.Compare(a, b) > 0 }
